    "metric_desc_cardiovascular": "Every step trains your heart like a muscle. Regular walking improves cardiovascular efficiency and significantly reduces your resting heart rate (HR) — a clear sign that your heart works better and with less effort. Fewer beats, less cardiac wear, and a lower risk of heart attack.",
    "metric_desc_endurance": "VO₂ max measures your aerobic capacity — how much oxygen your muscles can use during intense exercise. The higher it is, the better your performance and the lower your fatigue. Walking more increases your VO₂ max: the heart pumps more blood, the lungs absorb more oxygen, and muscles build more mitochondria — the cellular \"power plants.\" The result is a body that is more efficient at using oxygen and generating energy.",
    "metric_desc_concentration": "During sleep, the brain's glymphatic system clears toxins and consolidates memories. Sleep deprivation reduces key neurotransmitters (acetylcholine, noradrenaline), impairing concentration and decision-making. With 7–8 hours, your mind operates at 100%: sharp focus, strong memory, and rapid learning — with no \"brain fog.\"",
    "metric_desc_regeneration": "During deep sleep, the pituitary gland releases the largest daily pulse of growth hormone (GH). GH activates protein synthesis, rebuilding muscles, strengthening skin, and slowing cellular aging. With adequate sleep, you wake up renewed: recovered muscles, firmer skin, and a strong immune system. It is your natural \"nightly maintenance.\"",
    "metric_desc_cramps": "Dehydration disrupts the electrolyte balance (sodium, potassium, and magnesium) essential for controlled muscle contraction. Staying well hydrated helps prevent involuntary spasms. With adequate water and proper mineral balance, muscle electrical signals function correctly and cramps are reduced by up to 65%.",
    "metric_desc_collagen": "Real anti-aging — without expensive creams. Hydrating from within strengthens the extracellular matrix and protects collagen, the structural \"scaffold\" that gives your skin firmness, elasticity, and structure. With adequate water, collagen remains intact, fibers do not fragment, and skin appears firmer, more luminous, and with less noticeable wrinkles. Visible results in 3–4 weeks.",
    "metric_desc_kidney": "Your kidneys filter 180 liters of blood every day. Drinking enough water produces dilute urine (> 2 L), facilitates waste elimination, and prevents the formation of kidney stones (mineral crystallization), reducing their risk by up to 65%. Clearer urine = healthier kidneys.",

    "metric_optimal_cardiovascular": "Resting HR: 60–100 bpm (normal)\n50–60 bpm (athlete)",
    "metric_optimal_endurance": "VO₂ max: 35–40 ml/kg/min (good)\n> 40 ml/kg/min (excellent)",
    "metric_optimal_concentration": "100% cognition",
